Let  $\mathcal A(\mathcal S)$ is a skew-symmetrizable cluster algebra, and $d^{t_0}(x_{i;t}) = (d_1,\cdots,d_n)^{\top}$ be the $d$-vector of the cluster variable $x_{i;t}$ with respect to the cluster ${\bf x}_{t_0}$ of $\mathcal A(\mathcal S)$. Then


(i).  $d_k$ depends only on $x_{i;t}$ and $x_{k;t_0}$, not on the clusters containing $x_{k;t_0}$, where $k=1,\cdots,n$;

(ii).  $d_k\geq -1$ for $k=1,\cdots,n$, and in details,
\begin{eqnarray}
d_k=\begin{cases} -1~,& \text{iff}\;\; x_{i,t}=x_{k,t_0};\\ 0~,& \text{iff}\;\;x_{i,t}\not=x_{k,t_0}\;\;\text{and}\;\; x_{i,t}, x_{k,t_0}\in {\bf x}_{t^\prime} \; \text{for some}\; t^\prime;\\ \text{a positive integer}~, & \text{iff}\;\; \text{there exists no cluster } {\bf x}_{t^\prime} \text{ containing both }x_{i,t} \text{ and }x_{k,t_0} .\end{cases}
\end{eqnarray}
In particular, if $x_{i;t}\notin{\bf x}_{t_0}$, then $d^{t_0}(x_{i;t})\in\mathbb N^n$, that is, the positivity of $d$-vectors holds.

(Fomin and Zelevinsky [FZ3])


(i). (Positivity of $d$-vectors) If $x_{i;t}\notin {\bf x}_{t_0}$, then $d^{t_0}(x_{i;t})$ is a non-negative vector, i.e., $d^{t_0}(x_{i;t})\in\mathbb N^n$;

(ii). Each component $d_k$ depends only on $x_{i;t}$ and $x_{k;t_0}$, not on the clusters containing $x_{k;t_0}$;

(iii). $d_k=0$ if and only if there is a cluster containing both $x_{i;t}$ and $x_{k;t_0}$.
